WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.701
-Thank you so much for being on the show.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.968
-Nice to be here, Jimmy.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.934
-Larry, where do people recognize you most from?

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:07.934
Is it "Daily Show"?

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.100
-You know what? It depends.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.467
Because I have different buckets.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.767
But there are a lot of people that know me from

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:17.767
"Senior Black Correspondent."

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:18.968
I have to say "Senior."

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.601
-Senior. -Exactly.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:21.767
-Senior Black Correspondent.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.267
-Senior Black Correspondent.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.634
But here's what's great.

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:27.200
See, I'm not famous enough for people to think that I suck.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.400
Alright? That's the best level of fame.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.100
-Wow. -I'm only famous enough

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.367
so that the people that know me like what I do.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.934
-Yeah, no one -- -"Oh, Larry Wilmore.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.400
You were so great on 'The Office.'"

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.567
Thank you very much. Eh...

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:43.033
I created "The Bernie Mac Show" on TV.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.467
Some people may know.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.834
[ Cheers and applause ] There you go.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.901
-You won a -- -I won an Emmy.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.200
-You won an Emmy. You won a Peabody.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.567
-I won a Peabody Award, as well.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:55.501
Hey, man. You guys remember the show?

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.033
"Bernie Mac Show"? -I love Bernie Mac.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.367
-Bernie was fantastic, man. -I love Bernie Mac.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.434
-We won almost every award you can possibly win.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.467
-How fun is that. -Yeah, it was great.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.334
And then I got fired. So there you go.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.968
-You got fired? -It's true. True story, yeah.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.167
-Why? Just --

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.033
-That's how Hollywood works, Jimmy.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.601
-You win the award and then they fire you off the show?

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.534
-"Larry, we're done with you now." Yeah.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:18.133
It was funny, because, you know, Hollywood is just like this.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.133
But I took the high road.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.767
In the press -- This is true. I'm not making this up.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.667
I said, "You know, we had creative differences.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.167
I was creative, and they were different."

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:28.667
-There you go. One of the -- I like that. I like that.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.000
-Keep the high road, Jimmy.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.400
-Keep the high road, buddy. -Keep the high road, man.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.634
-I was doing a little research about you

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:35.801
because you were coming on

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.601
and I found something I thought was fun.

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:41.167
You had a recurring role on "The Facts of Life."

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.801
-I did. I actually did. This is a true story.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.234
Oh, my God. This is --

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.601
-I have a photo of you and Mrs. Garrett.

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:47.734
-Oh, man. -This is real.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.467
-There you go. It's true. -Look at Larry.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:50.968
Look at Larry Wilmore right there.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.234
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.834
-Wow!

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.634
-Wow. -That's a deep cut.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.868
-I know. -I love that show. Come on.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.534
-I love that I got the puppy "aww."

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:04.033
That was very nice. -Yeah, you got the "aww."

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.734
-I look exactly the same. It's amazing, isn't it?

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.234
-Were you doing stand-up during that?

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.434
-I was. I was doing stand-up.

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.234
It's so tough when you're starting out stand-up.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.434
Am I right? -Oh, it's the hardest.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.734
-You never know what's gonna make it.

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.000
So -- And, you know, when you're trying out jokes,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.801
you always want to hammock jokes, right?

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.901
So what you do is you have a joke that works,

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:22.968
then you have new joke, and other joke that works.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:25.234
New joke, 10 seconds at the most.

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.534
If it doesn't work, gone.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:27.834
Audience doesn't even remember it.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:28.934
-No one -- Yeah. -Right.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.167
I was trying out a bit. -Okay.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.567
-A bit is a little longer than a joke.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:36.267
-A bit is longer than a joke. -It is longer than a joke.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:38.634
You know where this is going.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.000
Bit can be 30 seconds to two minutes.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.567
Guess how long my bit was, Jimmy.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.667
So -- And I wore my contacts all the time.

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:47.968
This time I decided to wear my glasses.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.734
And I'm wearing a robe. I don't even know what the bit was.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.367
Why I was wearing a robe, I have no idea.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.033
It's just my memories -- -I'm embarrassed.

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.300
-I'm not making this up, guys. I bombed so hard.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.667
And the things are --

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.467
You know you're bombing in the first ten seconds,

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.534
but you can't leave the bit because it's a bit.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.400
-Yeah, and you're wearing an outfit.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.901
-Exactly. I'm wearing an outfit. And I'm wearing glasses.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:08.033
I swear to you, guys. My glasses started fogging up.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.067
I am not making that up.

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.300
-That's how embarrassed you were?

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.300
-Yes! It was flop fog.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.133
-Yes! -Not even flop sweat.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:20.234
Flop fog. I couldn't even see them.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:24.100
I could feel these waves of hate, like, coming at me, right?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.501
But, like, the Lord saved me.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:27.834
I couldn't see them and everything.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.334
And to make it worse, they hated me so much --

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:31.834
I was also emceeing that night.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.767
So guess who got to come back on stage.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.067
-"Remember the skit about the bath robe?

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.801
Yeah, that's not me. It's a different guy now."

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.801
-I know. There were like, "Why is this guy back?

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.868
We hate this guy. Didn't he get the message?"

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.300
-But look at -- But look at you now.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.734
Look at you now. Come on, bud. You're in a big movie.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.868
Let's talk about "Jerry &amp; Marge Go Large."

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.734
-Very exciting. Very exciting. -Great cast, by the way.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.267
Bryan Cranston. I love Bryan.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:55.334
Annette Bening. -Ah. Man.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.701
-It's drama. It's got comedy. It's heartwarming.

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.100
It's based on a true story.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.200
Can you tell everybody what the story is about?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.801
-Sure. It's based on this guy named Jerry Selbee.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:04.834
True story. You guys may have seen it on "60 Minutes."

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.167
He beat the lottery. He didn't cheat it.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:07.567
He beat it using math.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.968
And he got the whole town involved.

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:10.601
So he didn't do it for the money.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:14.434
He won the town like $27 million over like seven or eight years.

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:17.901
Unbelievable story. Bryan Crantson plays Jerry.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.968
Annette Bening plays his wife, and I play his accountant,

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.434
'cause the brother's got to count the money.

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.834
-Yeah, okay. Of course. Yeah.

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:26.167
-And it was just so much fun working with them, Jimmy.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:29.267
It was just great. -We were saying backstage --

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.100
I said the reviews have been great.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.067
And you said, it kind of feels good for people to go like,

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.701
"Hey, Larry, we need this." -I agree.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.133
You know, I was telling Jimmy I'm living in gratitude.

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:40.334
Now, I lost my brother last year to COVID,

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:42.200
and I said, "I've been trying to live in gratitude

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.434
this past year."

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:44.701
When I read this script, Jimmy,

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:47.634
it was the type of movie that I feel people need.

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:49.300
We just want to laugh at something.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.467
We want escape, right?

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.167
We want to feel good about something.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.367
-Yes, please.

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:54.901
-And something for the whole family.

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:56.667
You can go enjoy. You're laughing. And it's feel-good.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.801
It's about a community that's doing something together.

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:00.734
How different is that

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.567
than the world we're living in now, right?

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:03.701
Right? -Yeah, I know.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.400
-People are pulling for each other.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.934
It's such an inspirational story.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.367
It was so much fun to be a part of it.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.634
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.934
Here's Larry Wilmore in "Jerry &amp; Marge Go Large."

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:13.334
Take a look at this.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:15.901
-So you want to start a corporation?

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:17.434
-Bring in the whole town.

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:20.267
If we sell shares, we'll have more capital to invest.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.334
-Go big or go home. [ Chuckles ]

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.601
-Then we'll split the profits with the shareholders.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:26.434
-Everybody rides.

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.033
-Will you stop talking like that?

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.367
-Sorry. I'm just really into it.

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:31.200
-She's really into it.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.534
'Cause she knows it'll work.

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.701
-House always wins. -Stop it!

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.033
You really think people will come in on this?

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.167
-Yep. You did. -Yeah, but I'm a depressed

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:41.767
widower with nothing to live for.

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:43.601
-You want to buy more shares, then?

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:45.133
-Yes!

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:47.534
-[ Laughs ] Larry Wilmore, everybody!

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.901
"Jerry &amp; Marge Go Large"

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:52.300
premieres this Friday on Paramount Plus.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.367
Thank you for making us laugh. I appreciate it, buddy.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:56.601
Good to see you.

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:58.467
Muna performs after the break. Stick around.

